  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The Sanctus with the Benedictus, closing the Preface at the threshold of the Canon: the seraphim's cry of Is 6:3 joined to the acclamation of Mt 21:9. Rubric s01 abridges the 1962 rubric as transcribed by witness do (line 203), which prints the comma at Benedíctus that the apparatus declines for the sung text; the bell is carried by the narrative layer; the bow and the sign of the cross stand in the rubric itself. Benedíctus (w017) is tagged as the lexicalized adjective, not as the perfect passive participle of benedícere: both readings are open to the analyzers, and the adjective follows the corpus ruling at orationes.ave-maria w007 and w012.",
    "source": {
      "method": "Verified by collation against the independent witnesses below: zero substantive divergence. Three accidental variants (punctuation) adjudicated in the apparatus.",
      "witnesses": "witnesses/ordinarium.sanctus/",
      "apparatus": "witnesses/ordinarium.sanctus/apparatus.json"
    },
